---
to: slide-facts.md
sparql:
  rendered: |
    PREFIX cs: <urn:xaas:case-study:>
    SELECT ?slide ?claimId ?standing ?claimText ?evidencePath WHERE {
      ?slide cs:rendersClaim ?claim .
      ?claim a cs:Claim ; cs:claimId ?claimId ; cs:standing ?standing ; cs:claimText ?claimText .
      OPTIONAL { ?claim cs:supportedBy ?evidence . ?evidence cs:evidencePath ?evidencePath }
    } ORDER BY ?slide ?claimId
  emptySlides: |
    PREFIX cs: <urn:xaas:case-study:>
    SELECT ?slide ?noClaimReason WHERE {
      ?slide cs:noClaimReason ?noClaimReason .
    } ORDER BY ?slide
  unrendered: |
    PREFIX cs: <urn:xaas:case-study:>
    SELECT ?claimId ?standing WHERE {
      ?claim a cs:Claim ; cs:claimId ?claimId ; cs:standing ?standing .
      FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?claim cs:renderedBy ?anySlide }
    } ORDER BY ?claimId
---
# Slide facts projection

Generated from the case-study claims ledger via the cs: projection
conventions (cs:rendersClaim / cs:renderedBy / cs:noClaimReason). A
presentation pack exists (pptx-presentation-pack, pres:); a consumer maps its
pres:Presentation and pres:Slide onto cs:Projection with a bridge of subclass
axioms (see packs/greene-licensing-case-pack/ontology/cs-pres-bridge.ttl)
without touching this ledger. Gate 030 guarantees this projection adds no
claim: every slide fact below resolves to a declared claim; slides without
claims carry only their cs:noClaimReason.

## Slide facts (claims that render)

{% for s in rendered %}- {{ s.slide }}: [{{ s.claimId }} | {{ s.standing }}] {{ s.claimText }}{% if s.evidencePath %} (evidence: `{{ s.evidencePath }}`){% endif %}
{% else %}- (no rendered claims)
{% endfor %}

## Slides without claims

{% for s in emptySlides %}- {{ s.slide }}: {{ s.noClaimReason }}
{% else %}- (none)
{% endfor %}

## Claims omitted from the projection (omission is lawful; addition is not)

{% for c in unrendered %}- {{ c.claimId }} ({{ c.standing }})
{% else %}- (none -- every claim renders)
{% endfor %}
